# Contributing to {{ project_name }}

## Setup

Install Python {{ python_version }} or newer and [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/),
then run the following from the project root:

```bash
uv sync
```

Use `uv run` to run commands in the project's environment without activating it.
Developer tools are declared in `[dependency-groups].dev` in `pyproject.toml` and
installed by default. Use `uv add --dev <package>` to add a developer tool or
`uv sync --no-dev` to install only the project and its runtime dependencies.

## Development

Keep application code in `src/{{ project_slug }}/` and tests in `tests/`.
Add tests for changed behavior and regression tests for bug fixes.
Use descriptive module names and follow the existing typing and docstring conventions.

Before submitting changes, run:

```bash
uv run ruff format .
uv run ruff check .
uv run ty check
uv run pytest
```

Ruff handles formatting and linting; ty checks types. pytest runs tests using
`importlib` mode and enforces the coverage threshold configured in `pyproject.toml`.
Share test fixtures through `conftest.py` rather than importing other test modules.

Keep changes focused and describe the behavior changed and checks performed
in your pull request.
